cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use prevalence-kit in published work, please cite it."
title: "prevalence-kit: audit-grade prevalence measurement for Trust & Safety"
abstract: >-
  A command-line tool that turns a sampling plan and human labels into a
  prevalence estimate with an honest confidence interval, sealed content, a
  tamper-evident record of every step, and a stamped report. It pre-registers
  the plan by hash before any data is touched, refuses by name rather than
  printing a number it cannot defend, and lets an outsider verify a published
  figure from the sealed record alone. No AI touches the evidence or the
  estimate. The estimators are validated against R survey, R epiR, base R and
  Python svy; the interval coverage is demonstrated against a census truth on a
  public corpus.
type: software
authors:
